### 5. Revision Feedback
The feedback compares the source against the model. Use sections 3 and 4 to interpret every reference in the feedback below.

Structural Check
- [S1] STC8 failed: Each action node must have exactly one incoming and one outgoing edge. | Node `n5` has in=1 and out=0. | DSL: action(n5,"Send Denial To Customer")
- [S2] STC20 failed: Every non-end node must have a path to at least one end node. | Violations: n5 | DSL: action(n5,"Send Denial To Customer")

--- REFINEMENT INSTRUCTIONS ---
1. Address all listed issues, all individual issues, by making edits that resolves them, and touch nothing else. Do not hunt for, introduce, or fix any problem the feedback does not mention, and leave every unreferenced element (its id, text, and position in the flow) exactly as it is.
2. Ensure the refined process model conforms to the DSL grammar, and constraints described above.
3. Output ONLY the finalized, refined DSL model inside a standard markdown code block, with no introduction, reasoning, or explanation.

--- ADDITIONAL GUIDANCE ---
Be extremely cautious and conservative: only change the model when a feedback item is completely unambiguous and you are absolutely certain of the single correct fix from the description alone. If there is any doubt, vagueness, or more than one plausible interpretation, do NOT act on that item and leave that part of the model exactly as it is. Prefer making no change over risking an incorrect one; keep edits to an absolute minimum and never add, rename, merge, split, or reorder elements unless strictly and explicitly required. Returning the model unchanged is an acceptable and often preferred outcome.<|im_end|>assistant
